<description>Remove duplicate provider and add mock data for TRPC query</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { PlatformManagedUsersTable } from '../../../../packages/features/users/components/UserTable/PlatformManagedUsersTable';
import { trpc } from '@calcom/trpc';

// Mock the trpc hook
const mockTRPCHook = {
  useInfiniteQuery: () => ({
    data: {
      pages: [
        {
          rows: [],
          meta: { totalRowCount: 0 },
          nextCursor: null,
        },
      ],
    },
    isPending: false,
    hasNextPage: false,
    fetchNextPage: () => Promise.resolve(),
    isFetching: false,
  }),
};

// Mock the trpc object
(globalThis as any).trpc = {
  viewer: {
    organizations: {
      listMembers: mockTRPCHook,
    },
  },
};

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    oAuthClientId: {
      type: "string",
      value: "example-oauth-client-id",
      label: "OAuth Client ID",
    },
  });

  return (
    <div className="w-full">
      <PlatformManagedUsersTable
        oAuthClientId={state.oAuthClientId.value}
      />
    </div>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:

1. Removed our custom DataTableContext.Provider since PlatformManagedUsersTable already includes its own DataTableProvider
2. Added mock data for the TRPC query that the component uses
3. Simplified the component structure to avoid provider conflicts
4. Mocked the global trpc object with the necessary structure

This should resolve the error because:
1. We're no longer having conflicting providers
2. The DataTableProvider from PlatformManagedUsersTable will properly initialize its context
3. We're providing mock data for the TRPC query that the component depends on

The ActiveFilters component should now receive the proper context from the single DataTableProvider, and the map operation should work correctly on the initialized activeFilters array.

If you're still seeing any errors, please let me know and I can help adjust the solution further.

